  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "NieR Reincarnation's narrative is primarily delivered through Weapon Stories—unlocking weapon story chapters by leveling specific weapons reveals the game's lore, which is as important as the main narrative.",
      "Combat uses an auto-battle system with manual Ultimate skill timing; the key skill is knowing when to manually trigger Ultimates to interrupt enemy charge moves before they deal damage.",
      "The \"Cage of God\" story mode stages have significantly different difficulty from the combat stages—narrative chapters serve as the primary story progression while combat chapters test team power.",
      "Weapon Acquisition focuses on the active character's primary weapon type; characters deal maximum damage with their optimal weapon class, and mismatched weapons reduce damage output by 30–50%.",
      "The companion system (Mama) provides party-wide buffs on manual skill activation; learning Mama's skill timing relative to Ultimate rotations creates significant damage windows."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "NieRリインカーネーションのストーリーは主に武器ストーリーで届けられる。特定の武器をレベルアップして武器ストーリーの章を解放するとゲームのロアが明らかになり、メインストーリーと同様に重要。",
      "戦闘は手動アルティメットスキルタイミングを持つオートバトルシステムを使用。鍵となるスキルはダメージを与える前に敵チャージ技を中断するためにアルティメットを手動で発動するタイミングを知ること。",
      "「神の檻」ストーリーモードステージは戦闘ステージと大きく異なる難易度を持つ。ストーリー章はメインストーリー進行として機能し、戦闘章はチームパワーをテストする。",
      "武器獲得はアクティブキャラクターのプライマリ武器タイプに焦点を当てる。キャラクターは最適な武器クラスで最大ダメージを与え、ミスマッチの武器はダメージ出力を30〜50%低下させる。",
      "コンパニオンシステム（ママ）は手動スキル発動でパーティ全体のバフを提供する。アルティメットローテーションに対するママのスキルタイミングを学ぶと大きなダメージウィンドウが生まれる。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Understanding the Story Structure",
        "body": "NieR Reincarnation has two parallel story layers: the Cage of God main narrative (following The Girl of Light and Mama through the Cage) and the Weapon Stories attached to each weapon (standalone short stories exploring the weapon's origin and previous owners). Both are canon to the broader NieR universe. Progress main chapters for combat unlocks and weapons for lore; neither should be neglected."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Character and Weapon Synergy",
        "body": "Mid-game power comes from matching characters to their optimal weapon classes and then investing in Awakening (character enhancement via Memory Shards) and Weapon Enhancement (via enhancement materials). 4-star and 5-star characters each have \"class-level\" bonuses from reaching specific Awakening milestones. The Weapon Upgrade tree increases damage multipliers and unlocks additional passive skills; prioritize the primary damage dealer's weapon upgrade before support weapons."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Dark Cage and Colosseum",
        "body": "The Dark Cage provides the hardest combat challenges and requires specifically optimized team compositions. Each Dark Cage boss has elemental resistances and phase triggers that require matching elemental team compositions and precisely timed Ultimate cancels. Colosseum PvP uses asynchronous battle replays; study top-ranked party compositions from the leaderboard to understand current meta defensive and offensive strategies."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Skipping weapon story chapters—weapon stories are not optional supplementary content; they contain canonical backstory essential to understanding character motivations referenced in the main narrative.",
      "Ignoring character elemental affinity when building teams—mixing elements without a damage-type focus dilutes both physical and magical damage potential significantly in mid-game content.",
      "Spending gems on duplicate pulls for enhancement instead of new characters—character duplication for Awakening is expensive; it is more efficient to advance Awakening through Memory Shard farming from events.",
      "Not monitoring enemy charge move timing in manual combat—enemies telegraph charge moves with visual effects 2–3 seconds before execution; using Ultimate cancel during this window is the primary survivability technique.",
      "Rushing main story without completing side cage floors—side cage floors provide the primary source of Memory Shards (Awakening material); skipping them delays character enhancement for 3–5 chapters."
    ],
